# Move the head smoothly and wait until it has stopped and settled (the servos
# have no position feedback, so "settled" is a timed estimate).
# Angles in radians, following the URDF joints:
#   pan:  positive turns left (about +z)
#   tilt: positive pitches down (about +y)
# Values outside the head's limits are clamped. speed: rad/s, 0 = the default.
# A new goal, a /head/target message or a set_pose call replaces the running goal
# (it aborts with "replaced"); cancelling stops the head where it is.
float64 pan
float64 tilt
float64 speed
---
bool success
string message
# Where the head is now (commanded), after clamping
float64 pan
float64 tilt
---
float64 pan
float64 tilt
